{
 "result": "squeeze.py is built and verified as a plain LZMA wrapper (FORMAT_ALONE, preset 9e). It round-trips the samples and was accepted at baseline 5.4748. Three LZMA2 literal-context variants (lc=2/3/4) scored 5.493 to 5.498, about +0.4%, below the 3% win threshold, so the incumbent was kept. Remaining ideas are a preset-dictionary primer, which Python's lzma does not expose, and zlib with zdict, which is likely worse than LZMA on these sizes. I am stopping here to conserve energy rather than spend it on changes that are unlikely to clear the threshold.",
